# Mihr UI Component Architecture

## Base Class Pattern

All components extend from a base class (e.g., `MihrButtonBase`) that provides:
- Shared rendering stack
- Style resolution pipeline
- State management via `WidgetStatesController`

## Size Variants

Components support standardized sizes: `sm`, `md` (default), `lg`, `xl`.

```dart
enum MihrButtonSize { sm, md, lg, xl }
```

## Named Constructors

Use named constructors for variants:
- `.sm()`, `.lg()`, `.xl()` — size variants
- `.icon()` — icon-only (medium, square)
- `.iconSm()` — small icon-only

```dart
MihrPrimaryButton(onPressed: ..., child: Text('Save'))  // md default
MihrPrimaryButton.sm(onPressed: ..., child: Text('Small'))
MihrPrimaryButton.icon(onPressed: ..., icon: Icon(Icons.add))
```

## Style Resolution

Resolution order (highest priority first):

```
widget.style  >  themeStyleOf(context)  >  defaultStyleOf(context)
```

- **widget.style**: Per-instance override
- **themeStyleOf(context)**: ThemeExtension (e.g., `MihrButtonThemeData.of(context)`)
- **defaultStyleOf(context)**: Component-specific defaults

## Color Access

Components MUST access colors via semantic tokens only:

```dart
context.textColors
context.bgColors
context.borderColors
context.fgColors
context.componentColors
context.utilityColors
```

Never use raw `Color` values or `Colors.xxx` in components.

## Shadow System

Use component-specific shadow config (e.g., `MihrButtonShadows`):
- `MihrButtonShadows.standard` — outer xs + inner ring + skeuomorphic
- `MihrButtonShadows.flat` — no shadows (link/ghost variants)
- `MihrButtonShadows.subtle` — light outer shadow only

Override via `shadowsOf(BuildContext context)` in the base class.

## State Handling

Use `WidgetStatesController` for interactive states:
- `WidgetState.hovered`
- `WidgetState.focused`
- `WidgetState.pressed`
- `WidgetState.disabled`

Components may accept an external `statesController` or create an internal one.

## Container Pattern

Separate the rendering surface into a dedicated container widget (e.g., `MihrButtonContainer`):
- Handles background color, shape, border, shadows
- Supports outer and inner shadows
- Integrates focus ring via `focusOuter` shadows

## ThemeExtension

Each component family has a ThemeExtension for customization:
- `MihrButtonThemeData` — shape, shadows, sizes, per-variant style overrides
- Register in `ThemeData.extensions` via `MihrTheme.light()` / `MihrTheme.dark()`

## Documentation

All public members (constructors, parameters, methods, classes) MUST have dartdoc comments.
